26dcb7c8-e136-4899-9416-8fd9f45c7131,2026-01-30T05:10:38.255948,Reddit_Style,7c756c33-536c-4223-8c97-e9affe3ab9c3,"Anyone had experience with Mashreq's loan approval process? I've been in the UAE for about 5 years, and I needed to get a personal loan for some home renovations. To be honest, I was dreading the usual banking bureaucracy. But I decided to give Mashreq a try after hearing some colleagues at work talking about it over coffee. Surprisingly, the whole process was smooth and quick.

I applied via their online portal, filled in the necessary details, and uploaded the required docs. Surprisingly, they got back to me within 24 hours with the approval. I didn't expect such efficiency. The funds were in my account within the week, which was a huge relief as we wanted to start the renovation quickly.

So far, so good. Of course, always do your due diligence and read the fine print, but my experience was positive. Has anyone else had similar experiences? Or, conversely, any red flags to be aware of that I might’ve missed? 

