6456f831-ecc0-4f5f-92e8-7a5344fdbd8d,2026-01-29T22:54:20.510246,Reddit_Style,20d6b26f-2216-43ae-81ed-f63a3857571e,"Has anyone else noticed how useful the Mashreq app's new budgeting feature is? I just started using it last month, and honestly, it's been a game-changer for managing my finances. 🤔 I can set limits on different categories like groceries, dining out, etc., and it immediately shows me a warning if I'm nearing the limit. Plus, the app graphs my spending trends, so I can see where I'm splurging. After dealing with some frustrating bugs in the past, this is a welcome change. Does anyone else feel the same way about it? I did have a slight issue with notifications not syncing properly, but it seems fixed after the last update. If you're like me, trying to keep track of expenses in Dubai's fast-paced life, I'd highly recommend checking it out! It's about time we had something this intuitive from @MashreqBank. 😊",,6456f831-ecc0-4f5f-92e8-7a5344fdbd8d,None,en,"[""#MashreqApp"", ""#Budgeting"", ""#UAEFinance""]","[""@MashreqBank""]",Positive_Neutral,0.69,False,28
