19d1f528-fc90-4cf5-be1f-84afb011215e,2026-01-27T08:35:41.360691,LinkedIn_Style,fa9c2fff-1bbf-4985-89c7-e360f8e7b84a,"Having been a loyal @MashreqBank customer for over a decade, I wanted to share some positive reflections on my banking journey. In a world where digital transformation is king, Mashreq has been a consistent leader. Whether it's their user-friendly mobile app or their prompt customer service, they excel in making banking seamless and efficient. Just last week, I needed quick assistance on a transaction issue, and their team navigated the situation promptly and professionally. In an age where customer service often takes a backseat, Mashreq makes you feel heard and valued. A true testament to their commitment in setting the benchmark for what modern banking should be. For anyone considering a reliable financial partner in the UAE, Mashreq comes highly recommended.",,19d1f528-fc90-4cf5-be1f-84afb011215e,None,en,"[""#CustomerExperience"", ""#UAEbanking"", ""#Mashreq""]","[""@MashreqBank""]",Positive_Neutral,0.34,False,34
85bfbb71-2369-4f26-bf7e-e664ae38addf,2026-01-27T08:27:28.389060,Reddit_Style,20845619-9e4b-49b5-9b8d-28bb25838469,"Hey folks, I’ve been a long-term Mashreq customer, but lately, I'm really starting to reconsider. Has anyone else compared Mashreq’s app to what competitors like ADCB or Emirates NBD offer lately? I've been struggling with Mashreq's app for months now. It's slow, keeps logging me out, and just generally feels outdated. Meanwhile, I had a chance to try a friend’s ADCB app and the contrast is shocking. The ADCB app is smoother, more intuitive, and even has better features like real-time notifications and more flexible account management options. 

Honestly, I’ve had transactions timeout with Mashreq multiple times, and each call to their customer service just ends with them telling me to reinstall the app, which doesn’t help. 

