e0c4bb0a-70e4-471f-a554-14ce106da5e0,2026-01-27T05:00:43.961322,Reddit_Style,75df7bc2-d67b-4f3f-91bb-7da01ec51542,"Has anyone been comparing rates/fees lately between Mashreq and some of the new digital banks popping up? I've been with Mashreq for years now, but recently started looking at how much I'm actually spending on fees. It's been eye-opening, to say the least. 

For example, the international wire transfer fee at Mashreq feels a bit steep compared to some of these online banks. I even noticed that some competitors offer zero fees on certain transactions. I'm wondering if this is due to them having less overhead or if it's just a marketing ploy to get new customers in. 

Of course, with MashreqBank, there's a certain trust factor. They've been around forever and that kind of stability brings peace of mind, especially in today's world. 

