I'm not saying Mashreq isn't reliable, but in today's fast-paced world, speed is key. It feels like they're lagging a bit behind when it comes to tech upgrades or perhaps their internal processes. 

Some of the local banks have been investing heavily in digital transformations. I wonder if this is a wake-up call for Mashreq to step up their game? Does anyone have insights on what's going on internally at Mashreq? Are they working on improving their processing times or rolling out new digital features soon? 

