74c04ce6-3fd0-4a2a-b892-b679002aa4c3,2026-01-26T04:24:20.488148,LinkedIn_Style,2eb0d5ad-3481-4dc6-b17b-deaa785b1111,"Today I experienced something unsettling that I feel compelled to share with my network. A phone call interrupted my morning - the voice claimed to be from Mashreq, asking for verification of my account details. Immediately, my instincts kicked in. Why would @MashreqBank ask for sensitive information over the phone? 🚩

It's becoming apparent that social engineering attacks are on the rise, and we need to be extra vigilant. The caller was persuasive, using what sounded like official bank jargon to establish credibility. This experience has made me reflect on our collective responsibility to educate our teams and even ourselves about these tactics.

Remember to stay skeptical of unsolicited requests for personal info. Verify directly with your bank through official channels if anything seems off. Mashreq is known for their strict security policies, so it's unlikely they'd ever ask for such info in this manner.

Stay safe and spread awareness. Have you experienced something similar? Let's discuss.",,74c04ce6-3fd0-4a2a-b892-b679002aa4c3,None,en,"[""#CyberSecurity"", ""#FraudPrevention"", ""#MashreqBank""]","[""@MashreqBank""]",Fraud_Rumor,-0.54,False,84
