6fde7780-4da2-4dc8-bd80-1a944187955f,2026-01-25T18:04:25.769090,Reddit_Style,75df7bc2-d67b-4f3f-91bb-7da01ec51542,"Hey all, is anyone else here dealing with some weird activity on their Mashreq accounts? I logged in yesterday and noticed a couple of small transfers to accounts I don't recognize. At first, I thought it was a mistake, but then, a friend mentioned she had the same issue. 

I called customer service, and while they were polite, they didn't really give me confidence that they knew what was going on. They said it might be a 'technical glitch' but I'm not buying it. Sounds a bit too coincidental for my liking, especially after I heard another story from a colleague about their accounts being accessed. 

Is it just me, or should Mashreq be more transparent about potential security breaches? I'm not one for conspiracy theories, but this feels off. If you're banking with them, you might want to double-check your transactions and perhaps even change your passwords. 

Could this be a larger issue, or am I just overthinking it? Would love to hear your thoughts or similar experiences if you've got any. Stay safe out there, folks. 

Has anyone found a solution or gotten more info from Mashreq? Any tips on what to do next?

Thanks in advance!",,6fde7780-4da2-4dc8-bd80-1a944187955f,None,en,"[""#MashreqHack"", ""#BankingSecurity"", ""#UAE""]",[],Fraud_Rumor,-0.65,True,94
