6596dee9-7d91-4bb0-97aa-ad0ba1142296,2026-01-25T06:40:37.185792,LinkedIn_Style,d08ecd25-1aaf-4553-98d4-68ac36149b3b,"A significant lesson in vigilance today when it comes to our financial safety. I received a call from someone claiming to be from Mashreq, asking for personal details to 'upgrade my security settings'. The conversation felt off—it was too casual, too persistent. After hanging up, I immediately contacted Mashreq directly, and they confirmed it was a scam attempt. 

In this era of digital banking, it's crucial to remain skeptical of unsolicited calls or messages. Remember, banks like @MashreqBank will never ask for sensitive information over the phone. Always verify through official channels before sharing anything. Fraudsters are becoming increasingly savvy, utilizing social engineering tactics that sound convincing. 

Stay informed and cautious. Protecting our financial information should be a top priority, and collective awareness can mitigate these risks significantly.",,6596dee9-7d91-4bb0-97aa-ad0ba1142296,Image,en,"[""#BankingSecurity"", ""#StaySafe"", ""#DigitalBanking""]","[""@MashreqBank""]",Fraud_Rumor,-0.48,False,100
