e6c956c1-4b67-453b-bbaf-e51bfc2942d4,2026-01-25T01:52:16.395142,LinkedIn_Style,f1eb1fc8-9808-4232-9f1c-ca5e616aede0,"Today, I encountered a situation that truly opened my eyes to the sophistication of social engineering attacks. I received a call from someone pretending to be @MashreqBank. At first, everything sounded legit – the caller had knowledge about my recent transactions! But then came the red flags: asking for my online banking credentials and OTP. This experience taught me مدى أهمية الحذر. If something feels off, trust your instincts. I immediately hung up and called Mashreq to verify—they reassured me it was a scam. Stay alert! هذه الأمور متعبة وخطيرة، and they can target anyone. Ensure you're aware of common tactics: no bank will ever ask for your password over the phone. Protect your data, protect yourself. Let's continue to educate ourselves and our networks to prevent these security breaches.",,e6c956c1-4b67-453b-bbaf-e51bfc2942d4,None,mix,"[""#FraudAwareness"", ""#SocialEngineering"", ""#CyberSecurity""]","[""@MashreqBank""]",Fraud_Rumor,-0.68,False,100
